{"author":{"id":"609bf866d4a5d716c19faf5d617b3bf3de478230d29602d72aad5aa90a80466f"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1794600892,"nonce":"LRaOD5THRc+eXkdn9PMaSNKjZDg=","message":"A real hlwindow archive links beside the runtime and runs: committed locally as 9ec6c1f8 (not pushed).\n\nBuilt hlwindow 0.3.2 the way its release does (`cargo rustc --release --locked --lib --crate-type staticlib --target \u003ctriple\u003e`, plus `--features android-main` on Android) with the same nightly that builds libash_std.a. The iOS simulator archive is 6.9 MB, with 303 `hlp_\u003cname\u003e` resolvers and `xwindow_attach_pump` / `xwindow_run_turns`. A host `cargo build` of the same crate (all crate types) leaves the archive as LTO bitcode that `nm` cannot read, so use the per-crate-type command.\n\nLinking it whole beside the stock libash_std.a fails on both linkers with the same two duplicates, `rust_eh_personality` and `std::panicking::EMPTY_PANIC`: one copy of Rust's standard library from each archive. Apple's ld (ld-1266.8) has no option to accept a duplicate definition (`-allow_multiple_definition` is unknown, `-multiply_defined` is obsolete and ignored); lld has one, but an app's own Xcode or Gradle link would not pass it. So the fix is in the runtime: `scripts/localize_runtime.sh` makes the Rust-internal symbols of the runtime's own object local (3 of 743 globals: the two above and one more), and the release's iOS and Android jobs run it before stripping. It uses `nmedit` on Apple and the NDK's `llvm-objcopy` on Android, and is release packaging only, not part of the CLI.\n\nResult with the processed runtime:\n- iOS simulator: links (5.4 MB). A Haxe program calling hlwindow's `ClipboardItems.create()` (no window needed) prints `distinct=true`, `nonzero=true`, the interpreter's output with the host `xwindow.hdll`. The toy program still passes, including the absent-primitive case.\n- Android arm64: stock runtime fails with the same two duplicates from lld; processed runtime links (10 MB) and prints the same two lines on the emulator, exit 0.\n- New link test: `a_runtime_with_local_rust_internals_still_links_a_program`.\n\nNot checked:\n- Linux: the Android branch of the script ran here with the macOS NDK; the Linux release runner has not run it, and neither new release job has run at all.\n- A different rustc: hlwindow's own CI builds with stable, ash_std with nightly. Mangled std names carry a per-version hash, so they would not collide at all and the unmangled `rust_eh_personality` still would; localizing it covers that, but I only built both with one toolchain.\n- hlwindow and hlwgpu together: each is a Rust staticlib exporting `rust_eh_personality`, so the two collide with each other regardless of ash.\n- The system libraries a native archive needs are not discovered: iOS needed `-framework UIKit -framework Foundation -lobjc` and Android `-landroid -llog`, taken from rustc's `native-static-libs` note and passed through `ASH_LINK_ARGS`. There is no per-library way to carry them yet.\n- The Android link needed a stub `xwindow_main`, which is the entry glue still to be done.","files":null}]}